# Rayenna site — bilingual parity & mobile-first

## 1. Every user-facing change ships in English and Malayalam

Do not merge UI, copy, layout, or feature work that only updates one locale.

| Locale | Location |
|--------|----------|
| English | `src/pages/*.astro` (site root, trailing slashes) |
| Malayalam | `src/pages/ml/*.astro` under `/ml/.../` |

**Shared i18n** (update both `en` and `ml` when applicable):

- Nav, footer, chat: `src/i18n/ui.ts`
- FAQs: `src/pages/faqs.astro` + `src/i18n/faqs-ml.ts` + `src/pages/ml/faqs.astro`
- Blog: `src/pages/blog/` + `src/i18n/blog-articles-ml/` + `src/pages/ml/blog/`
- New routable pages: add path to `ML_ROUTES` in `src/i18n/ui.ts` when a Malayalam page exists

**Links:** Malayalam internal links use `/ml/contact/`, `/ml/solar-calculator/`, etc. (trailing slash). Use `localizedPath()` / `lang` prop from `Layout.astro` — do not hardcode the wrong locale.

**Copy conventions (Malayalam):** brand name **റയെന്ന** (not റയെന്ന്); prefer **ഹരിത** over പച്ച for green/eco wording.

**Exceptions (OK in one language only):** legal entity names in English, external URLs, form subjects, filenames, JSON-LD — unless the user asks otherwise.

## 2. Mobile-first + multi-device compatibility

Design and implement for **small viewports first**, then enhance with `min-width` media queries. Every layout/CSS/copy change must remain usable and correctly aligned on **all** of these:

| Device | What to verify |
|--------|----------------|
| Android phone | ~360–412px; touch targets; no overflow |
| Apple iPhone | ~375–430px; safe areas; hamburger nav |
| iPad | portrait + landscape (~768–1199px); tablet hero / grids |
| MacBook | ~1440–1800px+ CSS; full horizontal nav; side-by-side sections |
| HP EliteBook | **1920×1200 @ 125–150% Windows scale** → often **~1280–1536px CSS** (not “true” 1920). Nav may be hamburger or compact horizontal; ML text is longer and clips easily |

**EliteBook / Windows scaling notes (learned):**

- Do **not** assume MacBook layouts work on EliteBook — CSS width is reduced by DPI scale.
- Malayalam needs extra room (Noto Sans ML + longer labels). Prefer stacking or wider ML-specific breakpoints over `overflow: hidden` / `translateX` hacks that clip glyphs.
- Laptop hamburger (when shown) should look like a right-docked panel, not a phone sheet.
- Narrow media queries that stop at 1479px often miss EliteBook at 125% scale — use ranges that cover **~901–1799px** when targeting “laptop but not large MacBook”.
- Never “fix for EliteBook only” in a way that breaks phones/iPad/MacBook; scope ML laptop overrides carefully and re-check other breakpoints.

Also:

- Touch targets, readable type, and no horizontal scroll on ~375px width.
- Reuse existing responsive patterns; do not add desktop-only layouts without a mobile baseline.
- Verify hero, nav, forms, tables, galleries, and chat on mobile before considering a change done.

## 3. Checklist before finishing

- [ ] English page/section updated
- [ ] Malayalam counterpart updated (or explicitly N/A with user approval)
- [ ] `ui.ts` / FAQ / blog ML files updated if strings moved to i18n
- [ ] Mobile (Android + iPhone) layout checked
- [ ] iPad / tablet breakpoint checked where relevant
- [ ] MacBook desktop layout checked
- [ ] EliteBook / ~1280–1536px CSS (Windows scale) checked — especially Malayalam
- [ ] `npm run build` passes
